<title>USA: Celgene gets SelCIDs patent.</title>
<headline>Celgene gets SelCIDs patent.</headline>
<dateline>WARREN, N.J. 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Celgene Corp said it has been granted a patent for a series of drugs with the potential to treat a broad range of immune related disease states, including rheumatoid arthritis, non-insulin dependent diabetes, AIDS and cancer-related conditions.</p>
<p>This composition of matter patent covers a class of compounds known as SelCIDs (Selective Cytokine Inhibitory Drugs) which have been shown in in vitro studies to be potent inhibitors of tumor necrosis factor-alpha (TNF-alpha), it said. The overproduction of this cytokine has been linked to a large number of serious inflammatory disease states.</p>
</text>
